<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55503" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταφημ-ίζω</span></b> , aor. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εφήμισα</span>, 
			Dor.
		 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εφάμιξα</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>O.</u>
			6.56
		</span></i>:—
			Pass.
		, pf. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεφήμισμαι</span>
		(v. infr.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spread
				abroad, announce</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατεφάμιξεν
				καλεῖσθαί νιν</span> Pi.l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίμνη
				Μαιῶτις, ἣν μητέρα . . τοῦ Πόντου κ.</span>
			<i>made</i> it <i>known as</i> . . , Dion. Byz.<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταπεφήμισται</span>
			<i>it is rumoured</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				16.12.3
			</span></i>; of persons, <i>become notorious</i> or <i>infamous</i>,
			Vett. Val. <i><span class="en">
				118.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>assign</i> or <i>dedicate</i> to a god, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τοῖς θεοῖς καταπεφημισμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.10.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρόνος Ἀλεξάνδρῳ -ισμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Eum.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				4.156c
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
